% =======================================================
\section{Directional-Sea Stability Target}
\label{sec:sea3-stability-target}

The implementation is intended for oscillatory marine motion, not for an
arbitrary bounded specific-force sequence.  The quantitative source-word proof
of Sec.~\ref{sec:stability-widening-source-path} deliberately remains valid as
the stronger implementation-source envelope, but it can be much more
conservative than the physical deployment class because instantaneous source
bounds alone permit sample-to-sample combinations that no directional sea can
produce.  This section therefore states the stability result that the next
certificate generation is intended to discharge: stability of perturbations of
a physically admissible, oscillatory, multimodal directional sea family.

The result below is a \emph{conditional target theorem}.  Its composition
argument is complete once the listed SEA0/P1--P5 certificates are available,
but this manuscript does not claim that the new SEA0 directional-sea enclosure,
the SEA3 P3/P4 margins, or the 45-degree SEA3 P5 capture certificate have
already been constructed.

\subsection{Three-partition directional sea class}

Fix
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{M_{\max}=3.}
 \label{eq:sea3-mmax}
\end{equation}
For partition $r\in\{1,2,3\}$ let
\begin{equation}
 \lambda_r=(H_r,T_{p,r},\gamma_r,\beta_r,s_r)
 \label{eq:sea3-partition-parameter}
\end{equation}
collect significant-height contribution, peak period, JONSWAP peak-enhancement
factor, mean propagation direction, and directional-spreading parameter.  An
inactive slot is represented by $H_r=0$ rather than by a change of model
dimension.  Under the spectral convention used here, $\gamma_r=1$ gives the
PM limit of the JONSWAP frequency family.

The directional elevation spectrum is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 E(\omega,\vartheta;\lambda)
 =
 \sum_{r=1}^{3}
 S_J(\omega;H_r,T_{p,r},\gamma_r)
 D_r(\vartheta;\beta_r,s_r,\omega),
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-directional-spectrum}
\end{equation}
where each $D_r$ is nonnegative and normalized over direction.  The partition
energies are coupled by
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{H_s^2=\sum_{r=1}^{3}H_r^2.}
 \label{eq:sea3-total-energy}
\end{equation}
Thus a one-system sea, wind sea plus swell, crossing swell, and a
three-component multimodal sea all belong to one fixed-dimensional parameter
family.  In particular, the proof is not allowed to maximize all three $H_r$
independently while also holding $H_s$ fixed.

The sea parameters evolve through a compact transition relation
\begin{equation}
 \lambda_{k+1}\in\mathcal R_\lambda(\lambda_k),
 \label{eq:sea3-rate-relation}
\end{equation}
whose component bounds include physically justified limits on changes of
$H_r$, $T_{p,r}$, $\gamma_r$, $\beta_r$, and $s_r$.  Those rate limits are
theorem assumptions to be certified by SEA0; they are not fitted to the eight
reference simulations.

\subsection{Directional response and oscillatory source}

The spectrum of Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-directional-spectrum} is not converted to
independent Cartesian acceleration boxes.  Let
$G_{\rm imu}(\omega,\vartheta;\lambda)$ denote the certified directional
sea-to-CoG/IMU response family.  The corresponding matrix-valued source
spectrum is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \Phi_u(\omega;\lambda)
 =
 \int
 G_{\rm imu}(\omega,\vartheta;\lambda)
 E(\omega,\vartheta;\lambda)
 G_{\rm imu}^{*}(\omega,\vartheta;\lambda)\,d\vartheta .
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-matrix-spectrum}
\end{equation}
It retains the physically coupled cross spectra between the measured vector
components.

For deterministic certification SEA0 supplies an outward enclosure of this
family by an oscillator/shaping state or an equivalent hard finite-window
dynamic constraint,
\begin{align}
 x^s_{k+1}&=A_s(\lambda_k)x^s_k+B_s(\lambda_k)w_k, \nonumber\\
 u^s_k&=C_s(\lambda_k)x^s_k,
 \label{eq:sea3-shaping-system}
\end{align}
with the oscillatory blocks preserving phase continuity.  The compact SEA3
theorem domain includes this deterministic realization coordinate; over a
finite sea window we write it as the coupled history set
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 (x^s_{0:N_W},w_{0:N_W-1})
 \in
 \mathcal X^s_{\rm SEA3}(\lambda_{0:N_W}),
 \qquad
 \mathcal X^s_{\rm SEA3}(\lambda_{0:N_W})\ \text{compact}.
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-hard-realization-set}
\end{equation}
Equation~\eqref{eq:sea3-hard-realization-set} is not an independent disturbance
box and does not reopen SEA3 compactness.  It makes explicit the
phase/driver coordinate already carried by $x^s$ in the complete SEA3 source.
SEA0 must provide a machine-readable outward representation of this coupled
set, its phase-continuous transition, and the left inclusion of the physical
SEA3 realization family into that representation.  The statistical spectrum
of Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-directional-spectrum} constrains the sea family but does
not, by itself, supply a deterministic pathwise bound for
$\mathcal X^s_{\rm SEA3}$.  Consequently, neither a Gaussian confidence event,
spectral moments alone, a replay record, nor a finite seeded harmonic
approximation may replace Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-hard-realization-set} in SEA0/P3.

For an individual undamped oscillator, for example,
\begin{equation}
 \begin{bmatrix}q_{c,k+1}\\q_{s,k+1}\end{bmatrix}
 =
 \begin{bmatrix}
 \cos\omega h&-\sin\omega h\\
 \sin\omega h& \cos\omega h
 \end{bmatrix}
 \begin{bmatrix}q_{c,k}\\q_{s,k}\end{bmatrix}.
 \label{eq:sea3-oscillator-step}
\end{equation}
The actual theorem input is separated as
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{u_k=u^s_k+d^s_k,}
 \label{eq:sea3-perturbed-source}
\end{equation}
where motion generated by admissible changes of the three sea partitions is
part of $u^s$, while $d^s$ denotes bounded out-of-class/model-mismatch input.
The deterministic theorem uses a hard finite-window bound on this input.  A
probabilistic statement for random sea realizations is a later corollary; no
infinite-time pointwise bound is inferred merely from a Gaussian spectrum.

\subsection{Exact tuner reachability and source-language refinement}

The deployed measurement-only adaptation path remains inside the source:
\begin{equation}
 u_k
 \longrightarrow
 \text{WavePeriodEstimator/prior source}
 \longrightarrow
 \text{band variance/EMAs}
 \longrightarrow
 (\tau_k,\sigma_{aw,k},R_{S,k},T_{S,k}),
 \label{eq:sea3-tuner-chain}
\end{equation}
including the exact stage/commit and pseudo-update scheduler state.  Shipping
code uses the fixed $0.2$ Hz tuning prior until the existing
WavePeriodEstimator reports \texttt{hasUsablePeriod()}.  The same estimator
starts its moment statistics after $3/\lambda$, may qualify startup use no
earlier than $4/\lambda$, and additionally requires at least one current
estimated period of moment history.  Its stricter \texttt{isReady()} diagnostic
still requires at least $6/\lambda$ and the existing debiased-moment weight.
The tuner update for sample $k$ executes before the current sample advances the
WavePeriodEstimator, so a newly usable period estimate can affect the tuner no
earlier than the following valid sample.  Filter \texttt{TunerReady} and Live
entry require this startup-usable measured period, but do \emph{not} wait for
\texttt{WavePeriodEstimator::isReady()}.  SEA3/P2 must retain the prior-driven
and startup-usable estimator-driven source modes and their one-sample takeover
edge.

Denote the tuner memory by $z^t_k$ and scheduler/hybrid source memory by $q_k$.
The augmented exogenous state is therefore
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\zeta_k=(x^s_k,\lambda_k,z^t_k,q_k).}
 \label{eq:sea3-augmented-source}
\end{equation}
The SEA3 certificate must establish the sound language inclusions
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathcal L_{\rm actual\ sea}
 \subseteq
 \widehat{\mathcal L}_{\rm SEA3}
 \subseteq
 \mathcal L_{\rm current\ source}.
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-language-inclusions}
\end{equation}
The right-hand language is the existing correlated implementation-source
language; its frozen P2 semantics are not redefined.  Replay records may
falsify either inclusion but may not be used to construct the SEA3 language.

\subsection{Finite sea windows}

With two or three active partitions the modal frequencies need not be
commensurate, so no common wave period is assumed.  Let $T_W$ be a finite
\emph{sea window} and
\begin{equation}
 N_W=\left\lceil T_W/h\right\rceil
 \label{eq:sea3-window-samples}
\end{equation}
its sample count.  SEA0/P3 must choose $T_W$ from a certified
finite-window information condition, not from a replayed trajectory.  A
representative target is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\mathcal O_{k,N_W}\succeq\alpha_O I,\qquad \alpha_O>0}
 \label{eq:sea3-window-information}
\end{equation}
for every admissible SEA3 window in each fixed-dimensional Live mode.

Let $M(\zeta)\succ0$ be the source-indexed information metric and write
\begin{equation}
 V(e,\zeta)=e^\top M(\zeta)e
 \label{eq:sea3-lifted-energy}
\end{equation}
in local error coordinates, with the exact Cayley lift of
Sec.~\ref{sec:stability-widening-source-path} used for finite attitude error.
The key nonlinear endpoint certificate is the window-wise inequality
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 V_{k+N_W}
 \le
 \rho V_k
 +\gamma_sD_{s,k}
 +\gamma_nD_{n,k},
 \qquad 0<\rho<1,
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-window-dissipation}
\end{equation}
where $D_{s,k}$ and $D_{n,k}$ are hard energies over the window beginning at
$k$.  No one-sample decrease of $V$ is required; growth inside an oscillation
is allowed.

For the homogeneous finite-state part of one complete shipping word, write
$\Phi_N=M_W\Phi_0+d_W$, $J_N=P_N^{-1}$, and
$D_W=J_0-M_W^\top J_N M_W$.  Retain the nonlinear residual, reset, boundary,
and projection history as one same-history coordinate $w_W$, without splitting
it into independent event radii, so that $d_W=B_W w_W$.  Then the exact endpoint
energy difference is the full augmented quadratic form
\begin{equation}
 V_N-V_0
 =
 \begin{bmatrix}\Phi_0\\w_W\end{bmatrix}^{\!\top}
 \underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}
 -D_W & M_W^\top J_NB_W\\
 B_W^\top J_NM_W & B_W^\top J_NB_W
 \end{bmatrix}}_{L_W}
 \begin{bmatrix}\Phi_0\\w_W\end{bmatrix}.
 \label{eq:sea3-joint-word-master}
\end{equation}
If the correlated nonlinear graph is enclosed by quadratic sectors
$z_W^\top\Pi_jz_W\ge0$, $z_W=[\Phi_0^\top,w_W^\top]^\top$, it is sufficient
to find nonnegative multipliers $\lambda_j$ for which the outward full-matrix
test
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{-\left(L_W+\sum_j\lambda_j\Pi_j\right)\succ0}
 \label{eq:sea3-joint-word-sector-test}
\end{equation}
holds.  In active accelerometer-bias mode this test is on the full 21-state
matrix and retains finite-$\tau_b$ bias decay and every state cross term.  Each
suffix in $B_W$ contains every later shipping event, in particular each due
$S=0$ update with the actual applied anisotropic $R_S$.  Thus
Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-joint-word-sector-test} may neither eliminate $a_w$ or
$b_a$ nor replace the same-history graph by a packet-count or independent-box
bound.

The bias source and its initial cell satisfy BIAS0/1 in
Section~\ref{sec:mems-bias-preconditions}.  The full nonlinear graph uses the
corrected error recurrence, not a free GM replacement for $\delta b_a$.
A BIAS2 sector from Eq.~\eqref{eq:bias2-sector} may enter the master only
after its uniform positive separation premise has been verified on this same
graph.  Literature or stationary PSDs cannot supply that certificate.

\paragraph{Source and finite storage attachment.}
Membership of an individual word requires one witness in
Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-hard-realization-set}, its joint translational/rotational
output map, the frontend/tuner root and the BIAS0/1 physical-bias history.
These must generate the word's actual measurements, schedules and $P,H,R$
cells. A capture of those derived cells alone does not supply the missing
witness. The unspecified hard-driver set and joint response realization
must be supplied before this membership predicate is executable; this is
separate from qualifying an assembled accelerometer. Neither declaring a
zero true-bias root after capture nor assigning a SEA3 identifier proves the
same-source equality.

For any invertible source-indexed frames $T_j$, a finite change of coordinates
$z_j=T_j e_j$ preserves storage exactly only with the simultaneous transports
\begin{align}
 \widetilde P_j&=T_jP_jT_j^\top,&
 \widetilde f_j(z)&=T_{j+1}f_j(T_j^{-1}z),\nonumber\\
 \widetilde F_j&=T_{j+1}F_jT_j^{-1},&
 \widetilde Q_j&=T_{j+1}Q_jT_{j+1}^\top,\nonumber\\
 \widetilde H_j&=H_jT_j^{-1},&\widetilde R_j&=R_j.
 \label{eq:sea3-finite-storage-pullback}
\end{align}
Indeed, inversion of the covariance congruence gives
$z_j^\top\widetilde P_j^{-1}z_j=e_j^\top P_j^{-1}e_j$,
and substitution gives the finite-map identity. At a pure reset
$P^+=GP_JG^\top$, choosing $T^+=T^-G^{-1}$ removes that covariance
reset in the transformed coordinates. Subsequent prediction, noise, floor
increments, measurement rows and the finite physical map must still undergo
Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-finite-storage-pullback}. Keeping their old numerical
values while deleting resets is generally a different Riccati history.

Equivalently retain the shipping coordinates. For a homogeneous correction,
put $q=e-Ky$, $r=e^+-Gq$, and $b=G^{-1}r$, where $e^+$ is the exact
Cayley/projection output and $G$ uses that correction's own injection. Then
\begin{equation}
 (e^+)^\top(GP_JG^\top)^{-1}e^+
 =q^\top P_J^{-1}q+2q^\top P_J^{-1}b+b^\top P_J^{-1}b.
 \label{eq:sea3-finite-reset-storage-attachment}
\end{equation}
The last two terms remain in the joint nonlinear graph. Their existence is
an exact identity, not a contraction estimate. A zero-error tangent check
does not authorize dropping them or reusing later covariance cells after
changing a finite reset. Until this attachment and source membership hold,
an expanding diagnostic ratio does not falsify the canonical P4 inequality.

Endpoint contraction alone is not sufficient for a full-sample ISS claim.
P4 must additionally certify a uniform prefix-gain inequality: there exist
finite nonnegative constants $\kappa_V,\kappa_s,\kappa_n$ such that for every
admissible SEA3 window and every $0\le\ell<N_W$,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 V_{k+\ell}
 \le
 \kappa_V V_k
 +\kappa_sD_{s,k}
 +\kappa_nD_{n,k}.
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-prefix-gain}
\end{equation}
The full-window energies may be used on the right because they dominate their
prefix restrictions.  This quantitative bound is separate from, and stronger
than, merely proving that all prefixes stay inside the Cayley/source domain.
For a homogeneous prefix $\ell$, the augmented test replaces the upper-left
block $-D_W$ by $M_\ell^\top J_\ell M_\ell-\Gamma_\ell J_0$, with a finite
$\Gamma_\ell\ge1$, and uses only sectors valid for that prefix.  Strict
endpoint contraction does not require prefix contraction.  BIAS1 projection
compatibility and error/source-domain retention must hold at each prefix;
no future-event BIAS2 information may be used to justify an earlier chart.

\subsection{Main conditional stability theorem}

\begin{theorem}[Three-mode directional-sea regional practical stability and
finite capture]
\label{thm:sea3-regional-practical-stability}
Assume the following hold for both fixed-dimensional Normal-Live modes.

\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*),leftmargin=2.1em]
\item BIAS0 qualifies the sensor model and its residual/mismatch envelopes;
BIAS1 attaches the true bias and corrected-error history to the source,
including projection compatibility and physical continuation through hold and
H$\to$A.  Stochastic and calibration/model mismatch contributions remain
in the declared forcing energies.
\item SEA0 supplies a sound outward enclosure of the three-partition
directional sea class of Eqs.~\eqref{eq:sea3-directional-spectrum}--
\eqref{eq:sea3-shaping-system}, including the compact hard realization set of
Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-hard-realization-set}, its declared rate-bounded parameter
evolution, and its directional vessel/IMU response.
\item P1 places the execution in the declared Normal-Live operating branch,
including the current no-accelerometer-rejection condition and the declared
startup prior/estimator source split.
\item P2 proves Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-language-inclusions} while preserving the
exact deployed period-source mode, tuner, parameter-EMA, stage/commit, and
pseudo-update scheduler history.
\item P3 supplies bounded positive source metrics and a strict finite-window
linear information/contraction margin on every SEA3-complete window.
Its configured finite-$\tau_b$ matrices are retained at $\delta=10^{-18}$.
Any later change to those matrices requires a new quantitative P3 build;
qualification alone does not change the deployed time constant or process $Q$.
\item P4 verifies both Eqs.~\eqref{eq:sea3-window-dissipation} and
\eqref{eq:sea3-prefix-gain} for the exact nonlinear shipping word map on an
invariant inner funnel $\mathcal F_{\rm inner}$, with every prefix inside its
declared chart/source domain.
Any BIAS2 sector it consumes has a certified positive constant on the exact
same-history nonlinear graph, as required by Theorem~\ref{thm:bias2-separation}.
\item P5 proves that every admitted 45-degree entrance state reaches
$\mathcal F_{\rm inner}$ in at most $K_{\rm cap}$ samples while respecting the
hybrid obligations.
\end{enumerate}

Then for the capture time $k_c$ and every integer $m\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 V_{k_c+mN_W}
 \le
 \rho^mV_{k_c}
 +
 \sum_{j=0}^{m-1}
 \rho^{m-1-j}
 \left(
 \gamma_sD_{s,k_c+jN_W}
 +\gamma_nD_{n,k_c+jN_W}
 \right).
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-practical-iss-sum}
\end{equation}
For every $0\le\ell<N_W$, combining this endpoint estimate with
Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-prefix-gain} gives the explicit intermediate-sample bound
\begin{align}
 V_{k_c+mN_W+\ell}
 &\le
 \kappa_V\rho^mV_{k_c} \nonumber\\
 &\quad +\kappa_V
 \sum_{j=0}^{m-1}
 \rho^{m-1-j}
 \left(
 \gamma_sD_{s,k_c+jN_W}
 +\gamma_nD_{n,k_c+jN_W}
 \right) \nonumber\\
 &\quad +\kappa_sD_{s,k_c+mN_W}
 +\kappa_nD_{n,k_c+mN_W}.
 \label{eq:sea3-practical-iss-prefix}
\end{align}
If every post-capture sea window satisfies
$D_{s,k_c+jN_W}\le\overline D_s$ and
$D_{n,k_c+jN_W}\le\overline D_n$, then
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \limsup_{m\to\infty}V_{k_c+mN_W}
 \le
 \frac{\gamma_s\overline D_s+\gamma_n\overline D_n}{1-\rho}.
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-practical-ultimate}
\end{equation}
and Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-practical-iss-prefix} yields the full-sample bound
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \limsup_{k\to\infty}V_k
 \le
 \kappa_V
 \frac{\gamma_s\overline D_s+\gamma_n\overline D_n}{1-\rho}
 +\kappa_s\overline D_s+\kappa_n\overline D_n.
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-practical-ultimate-full}
\end{equation}
Uniform upper/lower bounds on $M(\zeta)$ then convert these energy inequalities
to a regional practical ISS bound on the error norm.  When both perturbation
energies vanish, the inner error converges exponentially at sea-window
endpoints and Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-prefix-gain} carries that convergence between
endpoints.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
P5 gives a finite $k_c$ with the state in the P4 invariant funnel.
Equation~\eqref{eq:sea3-window-dissipation} can then be iterated on consecutive
SEA3-complete windows because P2/SEA0 preserve source completeness and P4
preserves the funnel.  Iteration gives
Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-practical-iss-sum} with disturbance energies indexed at the
actual post-capture window starts.  Applying the certified prefix inequality to
the window beginning at $k_c+mN_W$ gives
Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-practical-iss-prefix}.  Bounded disturbance energies and the
geometric series give Eqs.~\eqref{eq:sea3-practical-ultimate} and
\eqref{eq:sea3-practical-ultimate-full}; uniform metric equivalence then gives
the corresponding error-norm statement.
\end{proof}

The theorem is called \emph{regional} because the present entrance set is
fixed at 45 degrees.  A semiglobal corollary would require the certificate
construction to succeed for every prescribed compact entrance subset of the
Cayley chart; that stronger claim is not assumed here.

\subsection{Shipping envelope used by the new certificate}

The SEA3 construction must use the current deployed clamps rather than the
historical wider proof envelope.  The source at this revision gives
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{@{}ll@{}}
\toprule
Quantity & Current bound\\
\midrule
tuning frequency & $0.03\le f_{\rm tune}\le1.2$ Hz\\
OU time constant & $0.02\le\tau\le12$ s\\
OU acceleration standard deviation & $\sigma_{aw}\le4$ m/s$^2$\\
$R_S$ scalar clamp & $0.15\le R_S\le100$\\
$S=0$ pseudo-update period & $0.005\le T_S\le0.150$ s\\
dynamic EMA horizon & $\le35$ s\\
Normal-Live accelerometer rejection & not admitted\\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
These are source-parity values, not fitted sea parameters.
